e from an authenticator app that I don’t remember setting up for my OpenAI account.\n\nAfter reading the last three comments here, I decided to try again today. From my existing ChatGPT session, I went to Settings and tried to add a passkey. This required identity verification, which brought up the same authenticator code prompt. When I clicked “Try another method,” I saw two authenticator app options, just as before.\n\nOut of frustration, I selected one of them and entered a code from the authenticator entry I use for GitHub. # I cant access my account. I didnt setup an MFA and I dont have a recovery code before I used to get a code through my email as an alternative way but now nothing else and it keeps asking for those to login. I even contacted support and I got no reply.\n\nalneyadi2 September 12, 2026, 10:03am 59\n\nbefore I could use use another method and get a code from my email I dont know why you removed this option\n\niatur.malaga September 14, 2026, 8:08am 60\n\nI have the exact same issue, and I’ve been dealing with it for a full week now with zero response from support. I’ve tried both the help.openai.com chatbot , which escalated my case to a human agent last week, still no response; and emailing support@openai.com directly, also met with complete silence.\n\nThis forum keeps accumulating threads reporting the exact same issue, yet there is still no official acknowledgment or response from OpenAI. This is unacceptable treatment of paying customers who rely on this service daily and are simply being left in the dark.\n\njenny3 September 14, 2026, 3:33pm 62\n\nI am not getting anywhere - received this which I am taking means they cannot help me but I will continue to pay??\n\nI understand that you’re paying monthly for your ChatGPT account and need to regain access so you can continue your work.\n\nUnfortunately, we’re still unable to provide an MFA reset for your account because we could not establish the account history required for this recovery process.\n\nI understand this is not the outcome you were hoping for, but the completed MFA recovery review does not allow us to proceed with a Support-assisted MFA reset for this account.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nChatGPT Enterprise और ChatGPT Edu के रिलीज़ नोट्स | OpenAI Help Center (https://help.openai.com/hi-in/articles/10128477-chatgpt-enterprise-edu-release-notes)\nciteturn1174search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; # 8 सितंबर, 2026 ...   * स्वास्थ्य सेवा का सार्वजनिक डेटा: चिकित्सा अनुसंधान, नैदानिक परीक्षणों, दवाओं की जानकारी, Medicare डेटा और सेवा प्रदाताओं के रिकॉर्ड के लिए स्वास्थ्य सेवा से जुड़े नौ सार्वजनिक स्रोतों में खोजें.\n\n# 1 सितंबर, 2026\n\n## ChatGPT और Codex के लिए स्वास्थ्य सेवा प्लगइन\n\nपात्र हेल्थकेयर के लिए ChatGPT और HIPAA-सक्षम ChatGPT Enterprise वर्कस्पेस अब ChatGPT और Codex में स्वास्थ्य सेवा के दो प्लगइन इस्तेमाल कर सकते हैं:\n\n  * स्वास्थ्य सेवा का सार्वजनिक डेटा: चिकित्सा अनुसंधान, नैदानिक परीक्षणों, दवाओं की जानकारी, Medicare डेटा और सेवा प्रदाताओं के रिकॉर्ड के लिए स्वास्थ्य सेवा से जुड़े नौ सार्वजनिक स्रोतों में खोजें. यह प्लगइन केवल पढ़ने के लिए है और रोगियों के चार्ट एक्सेस नहीं करता.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nLocked out of account, unauthorized MFA (authenticator) method, active subscriber, requesting escalation (Case #13159972) - #36 by Alex_Don - Support - OpenAI Developer Community (https://community.openai.com/t/locked-out-of-account-unauthorized-mfa-authenticator-method-active-subscriber-requesting-escalation-case-13159972/1390436/36)\nciteturn1174search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 weeks ago; Crawled: 2 weeks ago; # Locked out of account, unauthorized MFA (authenticator) method, active subscriber, requesting escalation (Case #13159972) ... Alex_Don September 1, 2026, 7:01pm 36 ... I still have an active ChatGPT session on my Android phone, but I can no longer sign in on another computer or through the ChatGPT web version because the account requires an authenticator one-time code that I no longer have access to.\n\n# Locked out of account, unauthorized MFA (authenticator) method, active subscriber, requesting escalation (Case #13159972)\n\nChatGPT Support\n\nbug\n\nAlex_Don September 1, 2026, 7:01pm 36\n\nCase #13213918 – MFA lockout still unresolved since August 14\nHi, I’m experiencing essentially the same MFA lockout issue described in this thread.\nMy case is #13213918. The problem began on August 14. I still have an active ChatGPT session on my Android phone, but I can no longer sign in on another computer or through the ChatGPT web version because the account requires an authenticator one-time code that I no longer have access to.\nWhen I select “Try another method,” the only option shown is “Google Authenticator or similar.” I do not have a usable SMS, email, push, or passkey alternative. I also tried enabling Text Message authentication and adding a passkey from my currently signed-in phone, but both actions require the same missing authenticator code.\nI originally set up MFA using Symantec VIP Access. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCodex Astra GPT 6 is absolutely terrible and not worth using - #10 by SubaruMike - Codex - OpenAI Developer Community (https://community.openai.com/t/codex-astra-gpt-6-is-absolutely-terrible-and-not-worth-using/1399757/10)\nciteturn1174search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 days ago; Crawled: 2 days ago; SubaruMike September 22, 2026, 8:32am 10 ... The agent had normal repository write access, so there wasn’t a filesystem-level sandbox preventing it from touching other files. ... It had the constraint in active context, acknowledged the constraint, and then selected a different unauthorized implementation.\n\n# Codex Astra GPT 6 is absolutely terrible and not worth using\n\nSubaruMike September 22, 2026, 8:32am 10\n\nThis one wasn’t just vague negative prompting or cross-session drift.\n\nThe task prompt was very explicit about both the goal and the boundaries. The core requirements were:\n\n  * public GitHub `master` is authoritative\n\n  * Windows and Linux must use the exact same source SHA\n\n  * Linux is a port/build of that master, not an independent branch\n\n  * the existing protected NPC data stays private and must not be published to GitHub\n\n  * use the existing build/validation/deployment process\n\n  * do not redesign validation, generated data, private-data handling, or deployment\n\n  * do not make unrelated source changes\n\n  * if the existing process blocks completion, stop and report the exact blocker instead of inventing a new architecture\n\n  * actual success was a working live Linux deployment, not just green build checks\n\nThe agent had normal repository write access, so there wasn’t a filesystem-level sandbox preventing it from touching other files. I was relying on the agent to follow the explicit scope of the task rather than requiring approval for every individual write.\n\nThe important part is that it was corrected during the same task. After it proposed putting the protected file into public master, I explicitly told it that file was private and already existed on the private server. It acknowledged that correction, then proceeded to create a new private-input/import system and modify validation, tests, and acceptance scripts anyway.\n\nSo for this specific incident, I don’t think cross-session memory or newly discovered abstractions explains it. It had the constraint in active context, acknowledged the constraint, and then selected a different unauthorized implementation.\n\nThat’s why I’m leaning toward instruction-following/scope-control failure rather than simply “the prompt needed more Do Not statements.” The prompt already told it what to do if it hit a blocker: stop and report it. It chose to redesign around the blocker instead.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nLocked out of account, unauthorized MFA (authenticator) method, active subscriber, requesting escalation (Case #13159972) - #51 by rahulbajaj0242 - Support - OpenAI Developer Community (https://community.openai.com/t/locked-out-of-account-unauthorized-mfa-authenticator-method-active-subscriber-requesting-escalation-case-13159972/1390436/51)\nciteturn1174search7 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 weeks ago; Crawled: last week; # Locked out of account, unauthorized MFA (authenticator) method, active subscriber, requesting escalation (Case #13159972)rahulbajaj0242 September 8, 2026, 2:49am 51 ... Don’t have access to MFA and can’t login again.\n\n# Locked out of account, unauthorized MFA (authenticator) method, active subscriber, requesting escalation (Case #13159972)\n\nrahulbajaj0242 September 8, 2026, 2:49am 51\n\nCase number: 14598318\nHaving the same issue as others. Don’t have access to MFA and can’t login again.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCatatan rilis ChatGPT Enterprise dan Edu | OpenAI Help Center (https://help.openai.com/id-id/articles/10128477-chatgpt-enterprise-amp-edu-catatan-rilis)\nciteturn1174search8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; # 3 September 2026 ...   * Data Publik Layanan Kesehatan: Telusuri sembilan sumber layanan kesehatan publik untuk riset medis, uji klinis, informasi obat, data Medicare, dan catatan penyedia layanan.\nKontrol berlaku pada klien dan platform yang didukung. Mengizinkan situs atau aplikasi tidak akan melewati kebijakan lain maupun permintaan persetujuan. Pelajari lebih lanjut kontrol terkelola untuk penggunaan browser dan komputer.\n\n# 1 September 2026\n\n## Plugin layanan kesehatan untuk ChatGPT dan Codex\n\nWorkspace ChatGPT untuk Layanan Kesehatan yang memenuhi syarat dan ChatGPT Enterprise yang mendukung HIPAA kini dapat menggunakan dua plugin layanan kesehatan di ChatGPT dan Codex:\n\n  * Data Publik Layanan Kesehatan: Telusuri sembilan sumber layanan kes